<title>SLOVAKIA: SLOVAK CHEMOLAK H1 NET PROFIT DIPS.</title>
<headline>SLOVAK CHEMOLAK H1 NET PROFIT DIPS.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for six-month period</p>
<p>ending June 30, 1996: (in million crowns)</p>
<p> Pre-tax result	   78.187 profit   vs  101.816 profit</p>
<p> After tax result	 46.912 profit   vs   61.090 profit</p>
<p> Operating result	103.852 profit   vs  142.192 profit</p>
<p>Result from ordinary</p>
<p>  activities	     78.032 profit    vs  102.058 profit</p>
<p>Result from financial</p>
<p>  operations		24.304 loss     vs   40.134 loss</p>
<p> Extraordinary result    0.155 profit   vs    0.242 loss</p>
<p> Operating revenues    891.978	    vs  964.397</p>
<p>Revenues from financial</p>
<p>  operations		14.943	    vs    5.001</p>
<p> Ordinary revenues	 1.516	    vs    0</p>
<p> Extraordinary revenues  0.160	    vs    0.253</p>
<p> Operating costs	 788.126	    vs  822.205</p>
<p>Costs on financial</p>
<p>  operations		39.247	    vs   45.135</p>
<p> Ordinary costs	   78.032	    vs  102.058</p>
<p> Extraordinary costs     0.005	    vs    0.495</p>
<p>Net profit</p>
<p>  per share (in SKK)     93.52	     vs  121.79</p>
<p> Total assets	  1,677.599	    vs1,539.258</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Chemolak a.s. Smolenice. The</p>
<p>company is Slovakia's largest paint producer. Its shares are</p>
<p>listed on the Bratislava Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-210-3687</p>
</text>
